Guard against NULL entries in ttm->pages[] during unpopulate.

amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate() walks ttm->pages[] and writes to
pages[i]->mapping without checking for NULL. When a GPU command fails
midway the BO can be left partially populated, and the cleanup path then
dereferences a NULL page:

  RIP: amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate+0x77/0xd0 [amdgpu]
  CR2: 0000000000000018
  RCX: 0000000000000000
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception

CR2=0x18 is offset of struct page::mapping, confirming pages[i] == NULL.

This turned every compute fault on this board into a hard machine hang
(4 in one session, with unclean shutdowns and data loss). With the check
the process dies but the machine survives.

The missing NULL check is upstream code, not distro-specific.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -1255,8 +1255,13 @@
 	if (ttm->page_flags & TTM_TT_FLAG_EXTERNAL)
 		return;
 
+	/* BC-250/gfx1013: pages[] can contain NULL when the BO was only
+	 * partially populated (e.g. a command aborted midway). Without this
+	 * check the kernel panics on NULL->mapping (CR2=0x18).
+	 */
 	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i)
-		ttm->pages[i]->mapping = NULL;
+		if (ttm->pages[i])
+			ttm->pages[i]->mapping = NULL;
 
 	adev = amdgpu_ttm_adev(bdev);
 
